---
import Legal from "../layouts/Legal.astro";
---

<Legal
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="Paper Clock's privacy policy. Your alarms and goals stay on your Android device."
>
  <article class="legal-document">
    <p class="section-label">LEGAL <span>PRIVACY</span></p>
    <h1>PRIVACY<br /><em>POLICY.</em></h1>
    <p class="legal-updated">LAST UPDATED · SEPTEMBER 3, 2026</p>
    <p class="legal-lede">
      Paper Clock is designed to be private by default. Your alarms, goals, and preferences stay
      on your Android device.
    </p>

    <section>
      <h2>THE SHORT VERSION</h2>
      <p>
        Paper Clock does not require an account. It does not collect, sell, rent, or share your
        personal information. It does not use analytics, advertising SDKs, or cloud sync.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>INFORMATION STORED ON YOUR DEVICE</h2>
      <p>
        To provide the app, Paper Clock stores the alarm times, repeat schedules, labels, linked
        goals, selected sounds, vibration preferences, and target dates you create. This
        information is stored locally in the app's private Android storage and is not transmitted
        to us.
      </p>
      <p>
        You can remove this information at any time by deleting alarms or goals in the app,
        clearing the app's storage through Android settings, or uninstalling Paper Clock.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>ANDROID PERMISSIONS</h2>
      <dl class="permission-list">
        <div>
          <dt>Exact alarms</dt>
          <dd>Used to schedule your alarms to ring at the time you set.</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Notifications</dt>
          <dd>Used for alarm-related notifications where Android requires them.</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Full-screen alarm display</dt>
          <dd>Used to show the alarm interface safely when an alarm rings.</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Vibration</dt>
          <dd>Used only when you enable vibration for an alarm.</dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>NETWORK ACCESS</h2>
      <p>
        Paper Clock is built to work offline. The app does not need an internet connection to set,
        schedule, or ring alarms, and it does not send your alarm or goal information to a remote
        server.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>CHILDREN'S PRIVACY</h2>
      <p>
        Because Paper Clock does not collect personal information, we do not knowingly collect
        personal information from children.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>CHANGES TO THIS POLICY</h2>
      <p>
        If this policy changes, the updated version will be published on this page with a revised
        “Last updated” date.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>CONTACT</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about this policy? Email
        <a href="mailto:me@jonaylor.com">me@jonaylor.com</a>.
      </p>
    </section>
  </article>
</Legal>
